From: bcloud <bcloud@localhost>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:34:53 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?zaya:=20fix=208B=20architecture=20=E2=80=94=20B?=
 =?UTF-8?q?OTH=20CCA=20attention=20and=20MoE=20in=20every=20layer=20(HF=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ZayaDecoderLayer)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The port used the base-era alternating structure (even=attn/odd=MoE),
silently ignoring half the weights. Zaya 8B runs both blocks per layer:

  residual = h
  h = input_layernorm(residual); attn = CCA(h)
  residual = (attn+hsb)*hss + (residual+rsb)*rss
  h = post_attention_layernorm(residual); moe = MoE(h)
  h = (moe+hsb)*hss + (residual+rsb)*rss
final: logits = emb @ norm(h)

- loader: create all tensors per layer; add LLM_TENSOR_POST_ATTN_NORM
- graph: rewrite zaya.cpp loop; EDA on every MoE; final norm only
- hybrid memory filter: recurrent state for ALL layers (was il%2==0)
- converter: both weight sets per layer, res_scale_hs naming, expert_count
  keys, add_bf16 shape[::-1], real HF tokenizer (BOS=2 EOS=106)

Validated: 8/8 top-1 agreement vs HF Zyphra/ZAYA1-8B, logits corr 0.897
(int4 container vs BF16), coherent chat generation.
